meta {
  name: registration
  seq: 1
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

docs {
  Student self-signup. Unauthenticated -- these override the parent folder's
  bearer auth.

  Whether a new account can log in immediately is one env var,
  `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED` in `server/.env`:

  | Value | Register returns | Login before confirming |
  |---|---|---|
  | `True` (default) | "check your inbox", no tokens | 403 |
  | `False` | tokens, same shape as login | works |

  Accounts created by a paid checkout bypass this either way -- they paid.

  The other route into an account is `POST /public/bookings/checkout/`, which
  creates one silently and emails a generated password. Registering with an email
  that already booked is refused; use the password from that email, or reset it.
}
